  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Mapping Landscapes in Transformation (2019), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 5 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 2,007 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Mapping Landscapes in Transformation by Thomas Coomans, Bieke Cattoor and Krista De Jonge was published by Leuven University Press in 2019. Conceptually, the work connects to Transformation (genetics), Geography, Computer science, Biology and Biochemistry.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 5 citations. Citations peaked in 2023 with 3 citing works. Notable citing venues include Archaeological and Anthropological Sciences, Journal of Archaeological Science and Landscape series. The citing works include 4 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 4 countries, led by Italy, Colombia and Poland.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 2,007 times via OAPEN.</p>",
